.TH MQPWD 1
.SH NAME
mqpwd \- list Slurm jobs related to a working directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mqpwd
.RI [ PATH ]
.RI [ FILTERS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists jobs whose WorkDir matches the directory or whose job name is declared by a top-level shell script in that directory.
The current directory is the default.
.SH FILTERS
.BR --this-dir ,
.BR --dir " " PATH ,
.BR --name " " NAME ,
.BR --contains " " TEXT ,
.BR --regex " " PATTERN ,
.BR --older-than " " DURATION ,
.BR --younger-than " " DURATION ,
.BR --time-left " " DURATION ,
.BR --state " " STATE ,
.BR --partition " " NAME[,NAME...] ,
and
.BR --latest .
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.BR --verbose
shows match counts;
.BR --debug
also shows intermediate records.
.SH SAFETY
This command is read-only and never cancels jobs.
